NVK for a macOS floor below 12: applied last with NVK_EXTRA_PATCHES=nvk-legacy-floor (build/build_nvk.sh, NVK_FLOOR=<floor>).
The device open no longer reads the main-port data symbol that only macOS 12 and later export; the window-surface
code and the memory stream check at run time for what arrived after the floor; and a build for OS X 10.11 defines
inside the library the two libSystem calls of macOS 10.12 that its Rust half binds (nvrm_floor_shim.c, empty at any
other floor). The release build does not apply this patch.

